# =============================================================================
# Houston dev secrets — template for .env.local (gitignored).
#
# One-time setup:   cp .env.example .env.local   then fill in the values below.
#
# SECRETS ONLY live here. Everything non-secret (ports, URLs, tokens shared by
# the whole team) is committed in .env.development — never redefine those keys
# here; the dev doctor refuses to boot if you do, so the team can't drift onto
# different stacks. The single exception is GW_PUBLIC_BASE_URL (a personal
# tunnel, see the tunnel block). Run `pnpm dev` and follow the doctor.
# =============================================================================

# --- REQUIRED ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase (GCIP) Web API key for the `gethouston` project — powers Google
# sign-in for the web app's cloud profile. Not secret in the browser sense,
# but kept out of git by policy. Get it from a teammate or the GCIP console
# (Google Cloud → Identity Platform → project `gethouston` → app settings).
FIREBASE_API_KEY=

# --- OPTIONAL (the doctor reports the effect of each, loudly) -----------------
# Seeds every dev engine with an Anthropic credential so agent turns work
# out of the box. Without it, connect a provider in-app per agent.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Connected apps (Gmail, Calendar, ...) via Composio platform mode — one
# project key (free tier at composio.dev → Project Settings → API Keys).
# Without it, integrations are OFF and the doctor says so.
# COMPOSIO_API_KEY=
# Event triggers (routines waking on Gmail/Calendar events) additionally need:
# COMPOSIO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Desktop "Report bug" button files to Linear. Without both, the button
# ERRORS with "Bug reporting not configured" — the doctor says so.
# LINEAR_API_KEY=
# LINEAR_TEAM_ID=

# Desktop-app login/logout in dev (Google loopback+PKCE). Without BOTH, the
# dev desktop runs account-less (the doctor says so). Values: Google Cloud
# console → project gethouston → OAuth clients → the "Desktop" client (same
# one release CI bakes), or ask Felipe.
# GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MICROSOFT_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=

# Public tunnel: the `tunnel` pane exposes the local gateway on a STABLE https
# hostname through a Cloudflare named tunnel (gethouston.ai is on Cloudflare).
# One-time: brew install cloudflared && cloudflared tunnel login &&
#   cloudflared tunnel create <name> &&
#   cloudflared tunnel route dns <name> <you>-dev.gethouston.ai
# GW_PUBLIC_BASE_URL is the one committed key .env.local may override.
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL=<name>
# GW_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://<you>-dev.gethouston.ai

# Slack channel (the personal assistant mirrored into a Slack DM): needs the
# tunnel above. Create the Slack app from cloud/docs/slack/manifest.json with
# that hostname and paste its four values. Without them the channel is OFF
# and Settings → Channels says so.
# SLACK_APP_ID=
# SLACK_CLIENT_ID=
# SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=

# Which engine the DESKTOP pane runs against (one window, one engine):
#   local (default) — the local host: terminal/files/local-models profile
#   cloud           — the local gateway: real sign-in + MULTIPLAYER in the
#                     desktop window (needs the GOOGLE_DESKTOP_* pair above)
# DEV_DESKTOP_PROFILE=cloud
